# TripSplit environment variables.
#
# The core app is offline-first and runs without any backend. Only the
# optional Funding feature talks to the funding server.
#
# Copy to .env and adjust only if/when a real external service is introduced:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# No API keys, database URLs, or authentication tokens are required today.

# Reserved for future backend endpoints. Leave empty for the offline-first MVP.
# TRIPSPLIT_API_BASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Funding service (optional, online-only feature)
#
# When pointing the app at a funding server, set the base URL at build time so
# secrets never enter the source tree:
#
#   flutter run --dart-define=FUNDING_API_BASE_URL=https://funding.example.com
#
# If unset, production builds default to the deployed funding backend
# (https://tripsplit-funding.onrender.com). Override only when running against
# a local sandbox or a different host:
# FUNDING_API_BASE_URL=
#
# The funding server's own configuration (RAZORPAY_KEY_ID, RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET,
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET, DATABASE_URL, ...) lives in `server/.env` — see
# `server/.env.example`. Those secrets are server-only and are NEVER compiled
# into the app or committed to the repository.